# A17 plan

Hypothesis: on private TCP-disabled Xvfb, after the process-owned V15 owner is SIGKILLed while exactly `a`, `d`, and Button1 are held, the outer recovery routine accepts the backend event envelope, reconstructs the fsynced owner ledger, verifies the exact service start generation is dead, confirms unchanged focus/active surface/geometry and pointer inside the surface, then releases only the three ledgered inputs and writes an fsynced emergency receipt that an independent observer can verify.

Scope: one new isolated Xvfb allocation only. No physical device, game, model, or full V39 effectiveness claim.

Decision: PASS requires all state gates and independently observed down/up transitions, receipt+ledger hash binding, no normal owner receipt, session alive during recovery, and clean Xvfb teardown. Otherwise retain the original failure class. Candidate once, retries zero, auditor once.

Allocation ID: `V39-V15-PROCESS-OWNER-XVFB-A17-20261012-01`.
